From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:59:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: sun55i: reload the primary VSU attr block on page
 flips

The primary channel writes the plane alpha to the VSU global alpha.
A page flip reloads only the OVL layer and para blocks of that channel.
An alpha change on the primary then reaches the layer but not the scaler.

Reload the primary VSU attr block on each page flip as well.

Build-tested only, no A523 hardware.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
index 9c0ec2ed2be9..c8eda517fd2a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
@@ -962,11 +962,12 @@ void sun55i_de_layer_update(struct sun8i_mixer *mixer, struct sun8i_layer *layer
  */
 /* flip-min: only a few blocks need reloading on a page flip.
  *
- * The primary UI channel (pipe 0) carries the opaque desktop framebuffer: a
- * page flip only changes its fb address, so just the OVL layer/para blocks are
- * reloaded. The overlay and cursor channels (pipes 1/2) are staged dynamically
- * by Xorg *after* the initial full reload (the cursor plane comes and goes,
- * moves, changes enable state), so ALL of their blocks plus the shared blender
+ * The primary UI channel (pipe 0) carries the desktop framebuffer: a page flip
+ * changes its fb address and can change its plane alpha, so the OVL layer/para
+ * blocks and the VSU attr block (glb_alpha) are reloaded. The overlay and
+ * cursor channels (pipes 1/2) are staged dynamically by Xorg *after* the
+ * initial full reload (the cursor plane comes and goes, moves, changes enable
+ * state), so ALL of their blocks plus the shared blender
  * must be reloaded on every flip to keep the shadow in sync with the hardware.
  */
 static bool is_fb_block(unsigned int i)
@@ -984,7 +985,8 @@ static bool is_fb_block(unsigned int i)
 	c = (i - SUN55I_DE_BLK_UI_BASE_IDX) / SUN55I_DE_BLK_PER_UI_CH;
 	if (c == 0)
 		return i == SUN55I_DE_BLK_CH(0, SUN55I_DE_BLKCH_OVL_LAY0) ||
-		       i == SUN55I_DE_BLK_CH(0, SUN55I_DE_BLKCH_OVL_PARA);
+		       i == SUN55I_DE_BLK_CH(0, SUN55I_DE_BLKCH_OVL_PARA) ||
+		       i == SUN55I_DE_BLK_CH(0, SUN55I_DE_BLKCH_VSU_ATTR);
 
 	/* overlay/cursor: reload the whole channel register file every flip */
 	return i >= SUN55I_DE_BLK_CH(c, 0) &&
